    description: "Three families get a channel they lack today, decided by the ruling-10 test -- does the family describe the USER'S world or the LANGUAGE'S.\n\nframeworks (107 files, the largest family): conventions, including in-house ones. Straightforward channel.\n\ndataflow_patterns: MIXED, and the channel is SECTION-SCOPED. The grammar section (node_type: assignment / write: left) is internal. But 9 of 20 files carry a library_patterns section of regex rows ('\\\\.append\\\\(' -> mutate) matched by method name regardless of receiver type -- a claim about libraries, which a user with an in-house collection type can legitimately extend. Granting the whole file would hand them the grammar rules.\n\nfunction_summaries: the channel it most needs and the gate it least obviously needs. Entries describe callees 'whose source is not analyzed' = dependencies. But the file's own header states the asymmetry: a wrong  verdict closes a branch that is really open and DELETES A REAL SECURITY FINDING. A user-supplied terminating summary IS a sanitizer declaration by another name, and verify_claims discloses NOTHING about function summaries today while CAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER already exists for the identical case. So a TERMINATING user summary must ride that caveat and its exit-3 contract; a propagating one need not, since it cannot silence anything."  # 177d
    fields: {}  # 177d
