  set:  # 1a17
    description: "Three families get a channel they lack today, decided by the ruling-10 test --\ndoes the family describe the USER'S world or the LANGUAGE'S.\n\nframeworks (107 files, the largest family): conventions, including in-house\nones. Straightforward channel.\n\ndataflow_patterns: MIXED, and the channel is SECTION-SCOPED. The grammar\nsection (node_type: assignment / write: left) is internal by the same reasoning\nas cfg_nodes. But 9 of 20 files carry a library_patterns section of regex rows\n('\\.append\\(' -> access_mode: mutate) matched BY METHOD NAME REGARDLESS OF\nRECEIVER TYPE -- a claim about libraries and idioms, which a user with an\nin-house collection type can legitimately extend. Granting the whole file would\nhand them the grammar rules as well.\n\nfunction_summaries: the channel it most obviously needs, and the gate it least\nobviously needs. Its entries describe callees \"whose source is not analyzed\" =\ndependencies, exactly where a user knows something hypergumbo cannot. But the\nfile's own header states the asymmetry: a wrong \"terminates\" verdict lets the\nwalk close a branch that is really open, which DELETES A REAL SECURITY FINDING,\nwhile a wrong \"propagates\" verdict only leaves an unknown unknown.\n\nA user-supplied TERMINATING summary IS a sanitizer declaration by another name\n-- it removes a flow the tool would otherwise report -- and verify_claims\ndiscloses NOTHING about function summaries today, while\nCAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER already exists for the structurally identical\ncase with its exit-3 contract. So a terminating user summary must ride that\ncaveat; a propagating one need not, because it cannot silence anything.\nGranting this channel without that gate would re-open INV-buzab's shape on a\nfresh surface."  # 1a17
