- op: discuss  # 3670
  at: '2026-08-29T04:41:29Z'  # 3670
  by: agent  # 3670
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3670
  clock: 4  # 3670
  nonce: '3670'  # 3670
  message: "DONE in two PRs: #621 (frameworks + dataflow) and #622 (function_summaries +\nthe caveat gate). dev at 640bfa5a17. Split deliberately, on this item's own risk\nanalysis: the first two channels can only WIDEN recognition, the third can\ndelete a finding, and bundling them would have put a safety-critical change\nbehind a routine one.\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE, behaviourally, per channel:\n  frameworks.d/         in-house framework 'acmeweb' loaded -> True\n  dataflow_patterns.d/  user library_pattern applied -> True\n                        user GRAMMAR row ignored     -> True\n  function_summaries.d/ user summary loaded, stamped user_supplied -> True\n                        _use_site_terminates credited it -> {'acme.audit.swallow'}\n                        clean taint verdict -> confirmed_with_caveats,\n                        kind user_supplied_sanitizer\n                        control with no credit -> no caveats\n\nTHE THREE FAMILIES ARE WIRED DIFFERENTLY BECAUSE RULING 10'S TEST ANSWERS\nDIFFERENTLY FOR EACH, and one shared rule would have been wrong for two of them:\n  * frameworks: a user definition REPLACES the shipped one whole. A\n    FrameworkPatternDef is a coherent unit whose detectors and extraction rules\n    are written to agree; half-merging two yields a definition neither author\n    wrote. Not an inconsistency with io_primitives, where rows are keyed by\n    qualified name and per-row merge is well defined.\n  * dataflow_patterns: SECTION-SCOPED to library_patterns. Grammar rows stay\n    internal by the cfg_nodes argument -- a wrong node type silently empties the\n    CFG and therefore the taint walk. Grammar keys in a user file are IGNORED,\n    not refused, so such a file cannot break a run, and a test pins that they\n    take no effect.\n  * function_summaries: channel + CAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER for TERMINATING\n    entries only. A propagating summary cannot silence anything and needs no\n    caveat.\n\nTHE ATTRIBUTION IS THE PART THAT WAS NOT A LOADER CHANGE. A sanitized flow still\nsurfaces as a finding carrying sanitized_by_user_supplied, which is how the\nexisting caveat knows what to name. A TERMINATED branch produces NO FINDING --\nthat is what terminating means -- so _use_site_terminates gained a collector\nrather than the verdict code gaining a query, following the escape_sites\nout-param already in that function. Purely additive: the bool return is\nuntouched and the collector defaults to None, so an installation with no user\nsummaries produces byte-identical verdicts to before.\n\nSCOPE LIMIT, STATED IN THE CAVEAT'S OWN TEXT AND NOT ONLY HERE: the caveat is\nRUN-SCOPED, not flow-scoped. With no finding to attribute it rides every\nconfirming TAINT verdict in a run where any user summary was credited. That\nover-discloses, which is the safe direction, but it is coarser than the\nsanitizer caveat beside it and should not be read as per-flow precision.\nPer-claim attribution is a larger piece of work and is NOT done here.\n\nTWO ERRORS OF MINE, CORRECTED, both of which nearly changed the outcome:\n  * I reasoned this needed a SCHEMA CHANGE to carry the attribution across an\n    artifact boundary and was close to deferring the whole arm. False:\n    cmd_verify_claims runs the walk IN-PROCESS and hands taint_findings straight\n    to the verdict logic. I had not checked before concluding.\n  * My first test helper built a summary that does NOT terminate.\n    _summary_terminates is a six-clause conjunction where any doubt reads as\n    \"no\", so param_to_return={} alone is insufficient; side_effect=True is also\n    required. The predicate was correct and conservative; the helper was wrong.\n\nSTILL NOT WIRED, and reported rather than left to be discovered:\ntaint_sources.d/ and taint_sanitizers.d/. Ruling 10's table calls their channel\n\"yes (exists)\", which is true of the --taint-sources / extra_catalogs mechanism\nbut NOT of the .d/ directory, which nothing scans -- the same gap\nio_primitives.d had before WI-talaz. catalog-inventory reports them as\ndeclared-but-unread and the init-catalogs README lists them under \"NOT yet\nconsulted\", so no user is sent to an inert directory. Worth its own item.\n\nThe WI-vafit inventory gate fired on all three channels, which is the pattern\nworking as designed: wiring a channel fails its tests until the inventory is\ntold.\n\nFull suites: 24,699 (PR A) and 24,711 (PR B), 0 failed. Ratchet clean at 669."  # 3670
